# Kubri Media — Project Rules

## Positioning

Kubri Media is a boutique B2B technical creator marketing agency.
Name: Arabic for "bridge." Kubri is the brand, Media is the descriptor.
Tagline: "Kubri - Your bridge to technical audiences."
Voice: structural, reliable, infrastructure - NOT flashy agency.
Audience: B2B SaaS and DevTool founders, heads of marketing, DevRel.

## What Kubri does

Kubri is a MANAGED SERVICE, not a software platform or marketplace.
It researches relevant technical creators, evaluates fit, negotiates,
coordinates briefs and approvals, manages publication, and reports back.
Creators produce the content. Kubri manages the partnership.
Never imply Kubri has proprietary AI matching, scoring, or a network
of specific creators. Illustrations are methodology, not a product.

## What Kubri does NOT have (do not fabricate)

- Client testimonials, case studies, or named client logos
- Campaign results, view counts, revenue, conversion numbers
- Years of business experience
- Audience statistics or engagement percentages
- Awards, certifications, partnerships, network size
- Guaranteed views, sales, conversions, or ROI
- Fixed prices or minimum budgets

Pricing is project-specific. If pricing must be mentioned, say it's
a tailored proposal. Never publish a number.

## Vocabulary

- SAY: "technical creators," "developer creators," "technical channels,"
  "creator partnerships," "campaign," "relevant audience"
- DON'T SAY: "YouTubers," "content creators," "viral," "drama,"
  "hack," "guaranteed results," "10x," "explosive growth," "unlock"
- "Influencers" — allowed ONLY in the Hero headline as the exact
  negating statement "Not generic influencers." Nowhere else.
- No emojis. No exclamation marks.
- HYPENS ONLY, NO EM-DASHES (—). Even when source copy has them,
  replace with a hyphen surrounded by spaces (" - ").

## Design tokens

- Background: slate-950. Cards: slate-900/40 base, hover slate-900/60.
- Borders: white/10 base, white/20 on hover. Indigo/30-40 for accents.
- Text: slate-100 primary, slate-400 secondary, slate-500 tertiary.
- Accent: indigo. Buttons indigo-500 → hover indigo-400.
  Eyebrows and highlights: indigo-400.
  Emerald-400/80 is the ONLY secondary color, and ONLY in monospace
  terminal output where green = "success." Never in UI chrome.
- Typography: Inter. tracking-tight headings.
  Eyebrows: text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-indigo-400.
- Corners: rounded-2xl cards, rounded-xl terminals/pills, rounded-lg
  buttons/chips.
- Spacing: sections py-24 md:py-32. Content max-w-6xl, side px-6.
- Motion: 150-300ms color/opacity transitions. 2px max hover lift on
  cards (duration-200). No bounce, no spring, no scroll hijack.
  Scroll reveals (if used): CSS-only via @supports (animation-timeline:
  view()) + @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference). No JS.
- Focus: focus-visible:ring-2 ring-indigo-400/50 on every interactive
  element. Buttons add ring-offset-2 ring-offset-slate-950.

## Ambient glow policy

- Max 5 ambient glow blobs across the entire page.
- Hero: 2 (existing indigo-600/30 + indigo-400/20).
- Section glows: up to 3 more (Solution, Process, Guardrails already
  have them). New sections do NOT get a glow unless replacing one.
- Glow blobs use bg-indigo-500/[0.05] to bg-indigo-600/30 (never
  brighter). blur-[100px] to blur-[140px]. Never on text.

## Do not

- No stock photos, no people, no illustrations of humans.
- No gradients on text or card backgrounds (only as single ambient
  glows and 1px hairline dividers).
- No new dependencies without asking.
- Only one route exists on the site: /. /privacy is the only approved
  exception (added Phase 8).
- Never touch docs/COPY.md without also rewriting the section it
  describes in the same commit.
- Never add "use client" to a component that has no state, effects,
  refs, or event handlers.
- Never add client-side tracking, analytics, or scripts.
- Never fabricate proof, testimonials, results, or partnerships.

## Centralized config (never hardcode URLs in components)

All external URLs live in lib/config.ts. Components import from there.
Adding a new external link = add to config.ts first.

## Structure

app/layout.tsx, app/page.tsx, app/globals.css
lib/config.ts
components/Navbar.tsx, Hero.tsx, CredibilityStrip.tsx (new),
Problem.tsx, KubriStandard.tsx (renamed from Solution),
Bridge.tsx, HowItWorks.tsx (renamed from Process),
WhyKubri.tsx (new), Conversion.tsx (extracted),
Faq.tsx, Footer.tsx
docs/COPY.md

## COPY.md workflow

- COPY.md is source-of-truth for the CURRENT rendered copy on the site.
- When a component's copy changes, COPY.md updates in the same commit.
- The master brief is upstream intent; COPY.md tracks what's shipped.
